update public.arc_demo_databases set body='{"id": "D11", "title": "Conversations", "home": "Granola (calls) \u00b7 Gmail (emails) \u00b7 web survey", "view": "document", "version": "2026.09.30-v2", "status": "Pre-written fictional demo document stored in Supabase. No live provider sync.", "path": "Demo shop/Conversations", "note": "", "rows": [{"id": "D11-001", "line": 1, "scenario": "seed", "type": "Granola \u00b7 call transcript", "content": "Indoor seed handling into an existing conveyor. Confirm the custom mating adapter before quoting. Customer states dry indoor use; no washdown. Existing conveyor remains outside scope."}, {"id": "D11-002", "line": 2, "scenario": "seed", "type": "Gmail \u00b7 request email", "content": "Please quote 1 hopper assemblies; capacity 3 m\u00b3. Confirm the mating opening and bolt pattern from the customer drawing."}, {"id": "D11-003", "line": 3, "scenario": "seed", "type": "Web survey", "content": "What is the project / RFQ reference? DEMO-RFQ-2026-09\nWhat problem should the hopper solve? Provide a stationary buffer above an existing downstream process\nHow will the customer judge success? Controlled gravity discharge, reviewed interface, accessible inspection and agreed acceptance checks\nNew installation, replacement or expansion? New hopper connected to existing equipment\nNew or returning customer? Returning fictional client; prior jobs H-101 and H-102\nWhere will the equipment operate? Cedar Rapids, Iowa \u00b7 fictional facility; exact site not supplied\nWho owns the requirements and clarifications? Fictional purchasing coordinator role; requests one bundled clarification email\nWho approves the mechanical interface and material choices? Customer mechanical engineer role confirms interface; shop engineer owns fabrication design review\nWho confirms operating and cleaning needs? Customer shift supervisor role confirms fill/discharge cycle, access and cleaning procedure\nWho approves budget and purchase order? Customer purchasing manager role\nWhich requirement / drawing revision governs? Initial RFQ; drawing approval required before release\nWhat approvals are needed before manufacture? Sales confirms requirements \u2192 engineer approves design \u2192 PM confirms sequence \u2192 Ops clears release \u2192 purchasing reviews acceptance recheck\nWhat product and grades will be handled? Dry seed\nWhat alternate products or seasonal variations occur? One nominated product per hopper; customer approval required before changing product or grade\nLoose bulk density and test method (kg/m\u00b3)? Prepared customer planning estimate: 650 kg/m\u00b3; no sample test supplied, engineering must confirm\nCompacted bulk density (kg/m\u00b3)? Unknown \u2014 confirm worst-case stored density\nParticle size distribution, fines and maximum lump (mm)? Unknown \u2014 obtain representative sample / sieve analysis\nParticle shape and fragility? Unknown \u2014 confirm breakage tolerance and sharp particles\nMinimum / normal / maximum moisture (% by mass)? Unknown \u2014 measure product and seasonal extremes\nProduct temperature range (\u00b0C)? Ambient product stated; numerical limits unconfirmed\nMeasured angle of repose and test conditions (degrees)? Unknown \u2014 sample test required; not a hopper wall angle\nWall friction / flow-function test available? Unknown \u2014 no validated flow test supplied\nAbrasiveness and expected wear life? Unknown \u2014 confirm sample and service conditions\nChemical compatibility, salts or corrosive contaminants? Unknown \u2014 obtain composition and compatibility evidence\nHygroscopicity, caking or moisture sensitivity? Unknown \u2014 confirm storage and moisture behavior\nKnown bridging, rat-holing or compaction history? Unknown \u2014 ask operations and review flow testing\nForeign objects, tramp metal or contaminants? Unknown \u2014 define upstream screening and rejection policy\nProduct SDS, technical data and sample references? Not supplied; request current customer-selected documents\nRequired nominal hopper volume (m\u00b3)? 3 m\u00b3\nRequired working / usable volume and freeboard (m\u00b3 / %)? Prepared working-volume target: 2.7 m\u00b3 with 10% planning freeboard; final geometry unverified\nMaximum stored mass and overload case (kg)? Planning full-volume product mass: 1950 kg, calculated in Python from assumed density; not a rated structural load\nRequired normal / peak discharge rate (kg/h)? Customer target: 2,000 kg/h normal, 3,000 kg/h peak; no validated flow performance\nTypical / maximum batch size (kg or m\u00b3)? Customer planning batch: 1,000 kg; peak surge to be confirmed\nIncoming fill rate and peak surge (kg/h)? Prepared customer target: 4,000 kg/h; upstream rating unverified\nHow often is the hopper filled? Prepared example: two to four batch fills per shift; customer confirmation needed\nOperating hours per day and days per week? Prepared customer plan: 8 hours/day, 5 days/week; seasonal overtime by separate agreement\nContinuous or intermittent duty; starts per hour? Intermittent batch loading and gravity drawdown; planned 4\u20138 cycles per shift\nMaximum residence / hold time (hours)? Customer target: empty by end of shift; overnight hold only with reviewed storage procedure\nRequired minimum controllable flow or turndown? Manual gate used for isolation; downstream conveyor controls rate, no calibrated turndown guarantee requested\nFuture capacity increase or alternate use? No larger future payload requested; reserve layout space only, subject to site drawing\nMaximum length \u00d7 width \u00d7 height (mm)? Customer layout target: 2,200 \u00d7 2,200 \u00d7 3,600 mm maximum; site survey pending\nRequired shape and geometry constraints? Stationary hopper concept; final geometry requires engineering\nFill opening size, shape and flange (mm)? Unknown \u2014 confirm upstream fill interface\nInlet centerline, offset and orientation (mm / degrees)? Customer preference: centered vertical fill; final offsets follow the signed interface layout\nOutlet clear opening and flange specification (mm)? 200 mm manual gate + custom adapter\nDischarge elevation above finished floor (mm)? Customer target: 1,200 mm above finished floor; conveyor interface must confirm\nBolt pattern, hole size, flange thickness and standard (mm)? Unknown \u2014 customer interface drawing required\nIs a custom transition / adapter required? Custom adapter to existing conveyor; customer drawing C-101 R1 required\nRequired wall angle and flow-test basis (degrees)? Unknown \u2014 engineer selects from product flow evidence\nPlate thickness / gauge by panel (mm)? Unknown \u2014 engineer determines from loads and fabrication rules\nWhich upstream equipment connects, and who owns it? Customer-owned bag / bulk transfer equipment; no load may be transferred without an approved interface design\nUpstream static / impact / vibration loads (N / kN)? Unknown \u2014 equipment supplier data required\nWhich downstream equipment connects? Existing customer process equipment; remains outside quote scope\nDownstream reactions, misalignment and thermal movement? Unknown \u2014 interface load envelope required\nMaintenance access and removal envelope (mm)? Customer planning target: 900 mm clear service aisle on one side; actual safe access requires site review\nDimensioned layout / drawing numbers and revisions? Prepared layout request L-01 R0; fabrication must wait for a dimensioned approved revision\nSpecified contact material / grade? Painted carbon steel\nFrame and non-contact material / grade? Engineer-reviewed frame material per prepared design\nContact surface finish / roughness requirement (Ra \u00b5m)? Not specified \u2014 confirm before fabrication\nExternal paint, galvanizing or passivation requirements? Finish follows prepared material selection; coating specification pending\nCoating chemistry, thickness and color (\u00b5m / RAL)? Unknown \u2014 obtain customer-approved finish specification\nWeld standard, quality level and weld map? Unknown \u2014 qualified engineer / welding coordinator to define\nContinuous welds, flush grinding or crevice limits? Unknown \u2014 hygiene and product requirements to determine\nVisual / NDT method, extent and acceptance criteria? Unknown \u2014 agree inspection plan before release\nMaterial traceability / mill certificates required? Customer to confirm certificate level and retention\nDimensional, flatness and alignment tolerances (mm)? Unknown \u2014 approved drawings to specify\nSeal / gasket material and compatibility evidence? Prepared seal candidate; exact compatibility requires review\nFastener grade, finish, size and locking method? Drawing-controlled; prepared M8 allowance is not a released specification\nReplaceable wear liners or sacrificial parts? Not included; confirm abrasion and wear-life requirements\nCover, lid, inspection hatch and weather sealing? Open top + service access\nSupport frame, mounting and anchorage arrangement? Anchored stationary frame\nLifting / handling points and certified lift requirements? Unknown \u2014 engineered handling plan required\nGravity, screw, belt, rotary valve or other discharge? Gravity discharge only in the prepared scope\nGate type and isolation function? Hand-operated slide gate for start/stop isolation; lockable handle requested for maintenance review\nManual / pneumatic / electric actuation? Manual; powered actuators excluded\nRequired fail-safe position and lockout provisions? Not applicable to manual actuator; lockout details require review\nPermitted product / dust leakage? Unknown \u2014 define acceptance criteria\nVibrators, air pads, agitators or other flow aids? Excluded; need requires additional engineering scope\nHow should bridging or blocked discharge be handled? Stop feed, isolate connected equipment and follow an approved maintenance procedure; no worker entry assumed\nCleanout / service opening and access arrangements? Reviewed access required; no entry procedure approved\nScreens, magnets or metal detection required? Customer retains upstream screening; screen specification and maintenance remain customer responsibilities\nRequired dosing accuracy and test basis (%)? No dosing tolerance requested; downstream customer equipment performs metering\nIndoor / outdoor and exposure details? Customer states dry indoor use; no washdown. Existing conveyor remains outside scope.\nAmbient minimum / maximum (\u00b0C)? Unknown \u2014 customer provides design extremes\nHumidity range / condensation exposure (% RH)? Unknown \u2014 do not infer from city or geography\nRain, snow, ice, washdown or flood exposure? Customer states dry indoor service; no rain or washdown\nWind / seismic design criteria and governing code? Unknown \u2014 site-specific structural review required\nFloor / foundation capacity and anchorage details? Customer scope; engineer must verify imposed loads\nSalt, fertilizer, chemical vapor or corrosive atmosphere? Unknown \u2014 customer to identify exposures\nDoor, aisle, crane and rigging access (mm / kg)? Customer requests delivery as a completed assembly if access permits; doorway and lift envelope still need measurement\nHeadroom, overhead services and lifting restrictions? Unknown \u2014 measured site layout required\nVoltage, phase, frequency and available power? No powered equipment included; future utilities unconfirmed\nAir pressure, quality and capacity (bar / L/min)? Not required by manual scope; confirm if options added\nCleaning water and drainage availability? Unknown \u2014 operations to confirm\nWho installs, anchors and connects the hopper? Customer-appointed installer; installation excluded\nWho commissions and trains operators? Customer and qualified installer; scope to be agreed\nCombustible / respirable dust assessment available? Unknown \u2014 customer hazard assessment and representative testing required\nMeasured Kst / St class with report reference (bar\u00b7m/s)? Unknown \u2014 no sample-specific test result supplied\nPmax, minimum ignition energy and test references? Unknown \u2014 qualified specialist to determine required testing\nOxidizer or reactive-material classification? Unknown \u2014 verify current SDS; oxidizers need specialist review\nHazardous-area / electrical classification? Unknown \u2014 customer and qualified specialist must establish\nVent, suppression or isolation design responsibility? Outside prepared scope; specialist hazard review determines needs\nDust extraction interface and performance requirements? Unknown \u2014 customer / specialist system scope\nWorker exposure controls and industrial hygiene evidence? Unknown \u2014 site-specific assessment required\nBonding, grounding and static control requirements? Unknown \u2014 qualified design review required\nMoving parts, pinch points and access guards? Manual gate pinch points and interfaces require risk review\nPlatforms, ladders, fall protection or confined-space issues? No platform / entry system included; site review required\nIsolation, lockout and maintenance responsibilities? Customer-approved procedure required before operation\nWhich codes, standards and jurisdiction apply? Unknown \u2014 engineer identifies applicable requirements; no certification implied\nPermits, third-party inspection or certification required? Unknown \u2014 customer / engineer to identify\nWho signs off unresolved safety / feasibility conditions? Qualified engineer and responsible customer role; cannot be priced away\nDry brush, vacuum, wet wash or CIP? Dry cleaning only; no washdown per stated request\nFrequency and allowable downtime? Prepared operations plan: dry inspection at each shift end; isolate before cleaning\nAgent, concentration, pH and SDS reference? No wet-cleaning chemistry in stated scope\nCleaning temperature / pressure (\u00b0C / bar)? Unknown \u2014 procedure limits required\nDrying method and residual moisture acceptance? Unknown \u2014 confirm before returning to service\nFood / feed contact, hygienic or sanitary design requirements? No certification asserted; customer to define applicable obligations\nAllergen / cross-contamination controls required? Unknown \u2014 product and site hazard review required\nProduct changeover sequence and acceptance criteria? Single product in prepared scope; isolate and clean before any separately reviewed product change\nMaximum residue and cleanliness validation method? Unknown \u2014 customer defines measurable acceptance\nHow are contact surfaces inspected and accessed? Customer asks for external visual access to outlet and contact surfaces; detailed access design unapproved\nHigh / low level sensors or viewing indicators? Excluded; optional requirement to be reviewed\nLoad cells, weighing accuracy and calibration? Excluded from prepared scope\nPLC, local controls, I/O and communications? No controls supplied in manual scope\nUpstream / downstream permissives and interlocks? Customer system responsibility; interface review required\nEmergency-stop integration and safety architecture? No powered controls included; site risk assessment governs\nCable trays, penetrations and protection rating? Not applicable to base manual scope\nRequired alarms and operator notifications? Not included; define if powered options are requested\nData logging, remote access or cybersecurity needs? No connected device or remote access in base scope\nRequired inspection and test plan / hold points? Customer requests dimensional and visual weld checks before finish, gate function after assembly and final photo record\nFactory acceptance test method and witness requirements? Customer requests five unloaded manual gate cycles plus dimensional checks; test acceptance criteria to be signed\nSite acceptance test and performance demonstration? Customer / installer scope to be agreed\nMeasurable throughput / flow / leakage acceptance criteria? Unknown \u2014 cannot warrant performance without agreed tests\nProof-load / structural validation requirements? Unknown \u2014 qualified engineer to specify; no test load assumed\nCoating, finish and weld acceptance criteria? Unknown \u2014 specification required\nCustomer inspection, notice period and attendance? Customer accepts remote review of final photographs for this example; request 2 business days notice of hold point\nDeviation approval and nonconformance process? Shop records deviation, stops affected work and seeks written engineer / customer disposition\nSerial numbering and component traceability? Assembly serial and job number on nameplate; link material certificates and final inspection to that job record\nWho signs the completed acceptance record? Customer technical role signs documented acceptance; purchasing confirms commercial receipt separately\nQuote due date and urgency? Prepared customer request: budgetary response within 3 business days after clarifications; not a shop promise\nRequired on-site date and installation window? Not committed; requested date recorded separately\nWhich milestones can move and by how much? Unknown \u2014 customer priority discussion required\nCustomer drawing approval turnaround (business days)? Prepared customer planning allowance: 2 business days to review each drawing issue\nPartial shipments or batch release allowed? Customer preference: complete assemblies delivered together; partial shipment needs written agreement\nCarrier, shipment mode and responsibility? Customer-arranged flatbed / enclosed freight as agreed after final envelope and mass are known; freight excluded\nShipping envelope, weight and road restrictions? Unknown until reviewed design / shipping plan\nCrating, wrapping, corrosion protection and storage duration? Customer asks for protected flanges, secured gate, wrapped loose parts and a packing list; final crate design unapproved\nWho supplies loading, rigging and unloading equipment? Shop loads by agreed lift plan; customer provides suitable unloading equipment and site rigging team\nTransit damage inspection and claims process? Customer records condition on arrival, photographs damage and raises carrier exceptions before receipt signoff\nSite storage duration and weather protection? Customer plans covered short-term storage under two weeks; drying and corrosion protection remain subject to finish review\nProject-system job setup and handoff owner? PM receives approved BOM, build plan and conditions after acceptance\nBudget range / currency and approval status? USD; customer asks for a base-scope price and separately identified options, no approved budget ceiling supplied\nFixed price, allowance, budget estimate or time-and-materials? Prepared estimate pending explicit review; no automatic commercial commitment\nDeposit, milestones and final payment? Prepared terms: 50% deposit; balance before dispatch\nRequired price-validity period (days)? Prepared quote validity: 14 days\nFreight, tax and duties inclusions / exclusions? Freight and tax excluded; no tax determination\nCustomer-supplied items and exclusions? Foundations, anchors, powered downstream equipment, installation, certification and production release\nWarranty expectations and exclusions? Not specified; agree written commercial terms\nStartup / recommended spares and service support? Customer requests an optional spare gate-seal kit and fastener list; not included in base quote\nInsurance preference and responsibility split? Discuss project policy versus minimal cover; premium TBD, no policy quoted\nHow are requirement changes approved and priced? Sales records change request and price/schedule impact; customer and engineer approve a new revision before affected work\nPO requirements, vendor onboarding and release conditions? Fictional purchasing team issues PO referencing quote revision and approved drawings; no actual order in demo\nCancellation, suspension and restocking expectations? Not specified; agree written terms\nCustomer drawings / CAD file references and revisions? Prepared response 